    "durationMs": 610726,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified against the spec.\n\n**What I built** (Rails 8.0.2 pinned exactly, Ruby 3.4.3, API-only, PostgreSQL via `DATABASE_URL` — verified connecting to the `bench` database):\n\n- **`app/models/link.rb`** — `code` (unique index, 4–20 `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`, generated 8-char code when omitted), `url` (custom validator: absolute http/https with a host), `clicks` (default 0)\n- **`LinksController`** — `POST /links` (201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}`, URL returned unchanged; duplicate custom code → 409; invalid url/code → 422), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /links` (`{items, total}` in ascending creation order)\n- **`RedirectsController`** — `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with `Location` = stored URL and an atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1` (verified 25 parallel redirects → exactly 25 clicks); unknown code → 404 JSON\n- **Malformed JSON** → 422 `{error: ...}` via a custom body parser plus `rescue_from` covering Rails' lazy-params parse path\n- **`start.sh`** — runs `db:prepare` then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (config.hosts cleared in dev so any test Host header works); README documents startup\n- Config reads everything from `DATABASE_URL`; no credentials hard-coded\n\n**Verification**: a 43-check curl suite covering every requirement (status codes, payloads, error fields, URL/code validation edge cases, ordering) passed; data and click counts survived a full server restart via `sh start.sh`. Test data was truncated afterward, the dev server is stopped, and the tree is ready for the grader to run `sh start.sh`."
  }
